/**
 Analysis of problem:
 array is perfect if after sorted:
 for any index i:
 a0 * ai >= a0 + ... + ai
 or equiv:
 (a0-1) * ai >= a0 + ... + a[i-1]
 
 Consider a0 fixed.
 Denote f[i, s] to be:
 number of perfect sequence with length i, sum = s,  maximum is m.
 
 f[i, s, m] =sum_o f[i - o, s - 0*m, m-1] *  C()
 TLE, optimize?
 
 New idea:
 condition is equivalent to:
 at any point in sequence:
 Delta <= a1(ak - k + 1) - ak
 ak >= k
 
 Equivalent:
 1. b1 + ... + bn <= a1
 2. k-th maximum >= n + 2 - k, or if k-th maximum = n+ 1 - k, all value below this equal n + 1 - k.
 
 Recursive:
 f (len, sum, max)
 // max is allowed max
 
 if allowed max is tight: a1 + max = len:
    check a1 = len, max = 0,
 
 allowed max not tight:
 Consider the occurences of max.
 f = \sum_o f(len - occ, sum - occ * delta, max - 1)
            
 */

int N = 200;
